--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,30 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## WebMCP
+
+Pages expose five browser-side tools to compatible AI agents:
+
+| Tool | Arguments | Action |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `search_articles` | `query` | Search titles and summaries; return article metadata and links. |
+| `open_article` | `slug` | Open a known article in the current tab. |
+| `get_reading_list` | None | Return the current session’s saved articles. |
+| `save_article` | `slug` | Save an article; repeated calls leave it saved. |
+| `remove_saved_article` | `slug` | Remove an article; repeated calls leave it removed. |
+
+The implementation uses the [WebMCP imperative API](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/imperative-api), preferring `document.modelContext` with a fallback to the earlier `navigator.modelContext` entry point. Use a browser that exposes WebMCP in a secure context (HTTPS or localhost). Browsers without the API continue to work normally; this app does not install a polyfill or an external MCP server.
+
+Tools register once per document, remain available across Astro client navigation, and read fresh data on each invocation. Registration uses an abort signal and rolls back on failure. Network requests honor the execution’s cancellation signal. Tools use the same session cookies and client services as the UI; reading-list changes notify mounted bookmark buttons and the reading-list flyout. No cross-origin exposure is configured.
+
+For example, an agent can call `search_articles` with `{"query":"cycling"}`, then use a returned `slug` with `save_article`. Input and request failures return an `error` field; cancellations reject the execution. The existing reading-list POST endpoint still toggles bookmarks, while PUT accepts `{slug, saved}` for explicit state updates.
+
+Run the automated checks with Node 24 or later:
+
+```sh
+npm test
+pnpm build
+```
+
+The Node tests exercise tool registration and execution, request cancellation, navigation validation, UI notifications, and reading-list endpoint behavior without opening a browser.
